flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1["Collect and visually inspect a sample of at least<br/>ten damaged inserts. Classify each by damage type<br/>(surface scratch, deformation, crack) and location<br/>on the insert."]
    box_2{"Is the insert damage consistent with incoming<br/>material defects present before assembly?"}
    box_3["Continue production with a different batch of<br/>inserts. Create a non conformance record for the<br/>affected batch and notify quality assurance team of<br/>the incoming material defect."]
    box_4{"Does the damage appear only on inserts processed<br/>through one supply conveyor?"}
    box_5["Inspect inserts from each supply conveyor separately<br/>and compare the damage rate and pattern to identify<br/>whether one conveyor is the source."]
    box_6["Empty the affected supply conveyor, inspect the<br/>conveyor guide rail and end stop for sharp edges or<br/>debris, and reload with undamaged inserts."]
    box_7{"Does the damage pattern indicate over pressing or<br/>mechanical impact at the assembly pressing station?"}
    box_8["Complete the following checks: 1. Collect damaged<br/>inserts from three consecutive assembly cycles. 2.<br/>Note the damage location relative to the insert<br/>geometry. 3. Identify the station at which each<br/>damaged insert was processed."]
    box_9["Check the pressing head alignment, pressing speed,<br/>and force limit. Adjust to specification and rerun a<br/>test cycle."]
    box_10{"Is the damage occurring at or after the<br/>reorientation unit?"}
    box_11["Jog the reorientation unit through one full cycle at<br/>slow speed and inspect inserts before and after the<br/>reorientation step for damage onset."]
    box_12["Inspect the reorientation unit gripper contact<br/>surfaces for burrs or incorrect clamping force.<br/>Replace gripper pads or adjust clamping pressure to<br/>specification."]
    box_13["Inspect the discharge robot gripper and the output<br/>holder rack slot guides for deformations or debris.<br/>Adjust or replace damaged gripper inserts."]
    box_14["Run ten slow speed test cycles and inspect inserts<br/>after each station to verify the root cause has been<br/>eliminated."]
    box_15{"Has the root cause of the insert damage been<br/>confirmed and the corrective action verified<br/>effective?"}
    box_16["Record the root cause, corrective action, and<br/>affected batch numbers in the quality log. Notify<br/>quality assurance team and restart production."]
    box_17["Escalate to the maintenance team with the damage<br/>characterisation sample for further investigation.<br/>Halt production on the affected line."]
    box_18["Complete the following steps: 1. Access the<br/>production tracking system and filter by current<br/>work order. 2. Set the time window from the last<br/>confirmed good inspection to now. 3. Export the<br/>serial numbers of all inserts processed during the<br/>fault window."]
    box_19[/"Refer to the production tracking system batch<br/>traceability procedure."/]
    box_20{"Were any inserts from the fault window released to<br/>downstream assembly or shipped to customer?"}
    box_21["Issue downstream quarantine notification and<br/>quarantine all suspect inserts from the fault<br/>window."]
    box_22(["End, Quarantine issued: quality assurance<br/>disposition and customer notification required"])
    box_23(["End, Notify maintenance team and quality assurance<br/>team. Procedure complete."])

